# Generated from: specs/11-add-live-smoke-a-lifecycle-verification-marker/requirements.md
Feature: Add LIVE_SMOKE_A lifecycle verification marker
  As a lifecycle smoke operator
  I want a root LIVE_SMOKE_A marker with documented exact content and a deterministic Node test of those bytes
  So that an end-to-end SDLC run can prove it created and verified a known artifact

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Root marker has exact bytes
    Given a repository checkout after issue #11 is implemented
    When root LIVE_SMOKE_A.txt is read as bytes
    Then the file exists
    And its complete byte sequence is "smoke-a-213" followed by exactly one LF byte and no other bytes

  @SCN002
  Scenario: README documents the marker
    Given the same implemented checkout
    When README.md is read
    Then it documents the root LIVE_SMOKE_A.txt lifecycle marker
    And it names the token "smoke-a-213"

  @SCN003
  Scenario Outline: Node contract test rejects missing or wrong content
    Given LIVE_SMOKE_A.txt is <marker state>
    When the focused live-smoke-a Jest test runs from scripts
    Then the Jest process exits non-zero because the exact-byte marker test fails

    Examples:
      | marker state                                      |
      | missing                                           |
      | present with bytes "smoke-a-213" and no newline  |
      | present with bytes "smoke-a-213\n\n"            |
      | present with bytes "smoke-a-214\n"              |
